==English==

===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:conteinen<ety:bor<fro:contenir>>|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|conteinen}}, borrowed from {{der|en|fro|contenir}}, from {{der|en|la|continēre||to hold or keep together, comprise, contain}}, combined form of {{m|la|con-||together}} + {{m|la|teneō||to hold}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|kən-tānʹ}}, {{IPA|en|/kənˈteɪn/}}
* {{audio|en|en-ca-contain.ogg|a=CA}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪn|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|con|tain}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[hold]] [[inside]].
#: {{ux|en|The brown box '''contains''' three stacks of books.}}
#: {{ux|en|a spray bottle '''contain'''ing water.}}
#* {{RQ:Besant Ivory Gate|chapter=III|passage=At half-past nine on this Saturday evening, the parlour of the Salutation Inn, High Holborn, '''contained''' most of its customary visitors. {{...}} In former days every tavern of repute kept such a room for its own select circle, a club, or society, of habitués, who met every evening, for a pipe and a cheerful glass.}}
#* {{RQ:Economist|date=2013-07-20|volume=408|issue=8845
|title=[http://www.economist.com/news/science-and-technology/21581981-what-pollution-some-opportunity-others-welcome-plastisphere Welcome to the plastisphere]
|passage=[The researchers] noticed many of their pieces of [plastic marine] debris sported surface pits around two microns across. Such pits are about the size of a bacterial cell. Closer examination showed that some of these pits did, indeed, '''contain''' bacteria,{{nb...}}.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[include]] as a [[part]].
#: {{ux|en|Most of the meals they offer '''contain''' meat.}}
#* {{RQ:Economist|date=2014-04-21|volume=411|issue=8884
|title=[http://www.economist.com/news/science-and-technology/21601233-exploring-link-between-manganese-and-parkinsons-disease-subtle-effects Subtle effects]
|passage=Manganism has been known about since the 19th century, when miners exposed to ores '''containing''' manganese, a silvery metal, began to totter, slur their speech and behave like someone inebriated.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To put [[constraint]]s upon; to [[restrain]]; to [[confine]]; to [[keep]] [[within]] [[bounds]].
#: {{ux|en|I'm so excited, I can hardly '''contain''' myself!}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Taming of the Shrew|act=Induction|scene=i|passage=Fear not, my lord: we can '''contain''' ourselves.}}
#* {{RQ:Spenser Ireland
|passage=[The king's] only Person is oftentimes instead of an Army, to '''contain''' the unruly People from a thousand evil Occasions.}}
#* {{RQ:Besant Ivory Gate|chapter=Prologue|page=16|passage=Athelstan Arundel walked home all the way, foaming and raging. No omnibus, cab, or conveyance ever built could '''contain''' a young man in such a rage. His mother lived at Pembridge Square, which is four good measured miles from Lincoln's Inn.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|author=w:Lee Mavers|authorlabel=no|title={{w|There She Goes (The La's song)|There She Goes}}|album={{w|Sixpence None the Richer (album)|Sixpence None the Richer}}|date=|year=1988|year_published=1997|artist=w:Sixpence None the Richer|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=68MKLkNSMN4|text=There she goes / There she goes again / Racing through my brain / And I just can't '''contain''' / This feeling that remains}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics|of a [[set]] etc.|transitive}} To have as an [[element]] or [[subset]].
#: {{ux|en|A group '''contains''' a unique inverse for each of its elements.}}
#: {{ux|en|If that subgraph '''contains''' the vertex in question then it must be spanning.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|intransitive}} To [[restrain]] [[desire]]; to live in [[continence]] or [[chastity]].
#* {{RQ:KJV|Bible|1 Corinthians|8|9|passage=But if they cannot '''contain''', let them marry.}}

====Usage notes====
* This is generally a [[stative verb]] that rarely takes the continuous inflection. See [[:Category:English stative verbs]]

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|hold inside}} {{l|en|enclose}}, {{l|en|inhold}}
* {{sense|include as part}} {{l|en|comprise}}, {{l|en|embody}}, {{l|en|incorporate}}, {{l|en|inhold}}
* {{sense|limit by restraint}} {{l|en|control}}, {{l|en|curb}}, {{l|en|repress}}, {{l|en|restrain}}, {{l|en|restrict}}, {{l|en|stifle}}; See also [[Thesaurus:curb]]

====Antonyms====
* {{antsense|include as part}} {{l|en|exclude}}, {{l|en|omit}}
* {{antsense|limit by restraint}} {{l|en|release}}, {{l|en|vent}}

